+# Shaft ROI v2 coordinate contract
+
+The accepted bundle is a bounded annular shaft chart, with **h ∈ [0.14, 0.94]**,
+periodic theta in radians, and d ∈ [0, 1]. d=0 is the actual outer boundary
+of the stored tetrahedra; d=1 is the inner shell at radial fraction 0.04.
+The centerline and the two excluded end regions are outside this chart.
+
+Only d solves a positive-edge-weight **discrete graph Laplace** problem.
+h is a transported centerline station label and theta is a periodic angle in
+parallel-transport frames. This is not a theorem about a three-scalar harmonic
+map, and a scalar maximum principle does not imply coordinate injectivity.
+The released bundle passed separate spatial and material-domain audits.
+
+## Load, query, invert
+
+Use the frozen `shaft_roi_v2/atlas_right.npz` or `atlas_left.npz` and its matching
+`attachments_{side}.npz`; paths and hashes are in the bundle manifest.
+
+```python
+from projects.genesis_ue_sync.anatomy_retarget.leg_volume_coordinates.atlas import (
+    load_leg_volume_atlas, query_atlas_coordinates,
+)
+from projects.genesis_ue_sync.anatomy_retarget.leg_volume_coordinates.volume_refine import VolumeTetRefiner
+
+atlas = load_leg_volume_atlas(atlas_path)
+refiner = VolumeTetRefiner.from_atlas(atlas)
+point_can = refiner.xi_to_p([[1.2, 0.5, 0.5]])
+xi, skin_chart_sample = query_atlas_coordinates(atlas, point_can)
+```
+
+The v2 asset declares baked native-tetrahedral queries as its default. Both
+forward and inverse reject unsupported positions/addresses and ambiguous
+cells. Theta wraps periodically; invalid h/d are never clipped to a boundary.
+Physical point inputs and inverse outputs retain float64 so valid triangle
+interiors remain on the actual boundary. Scalar fields and stored vertices
+retain the existing float32 atlas format.
+
+Legacy assets without a declared default continue to use the separately named
+skin/core distance-ratio depth field. It is not the baked graph solution.
+
+## DMP integration entry
+
+Run from the Among_US repository:
+
+```bash
+python -m DMP_playground.run_volume_coordinate_query \
+  --config DMP_playground/configs/shaft_roi_v2_20261110.json \
+  --xi 1.2 0.5 0.5 --knee-deg 60
+```
+
+The explicit configuration selects the new coordinate bundle and verifies its
+asset/attachment hashes. It uses the actual DMP configuration and canonical
+SMPL-X bundle loaders, evaluates fixed node attachments, and transports the
+point through its native tetrahedron before querying the posed chart.
+
+`volume_lbs_weights` is fixed across poses. Outer attachments inherit the
+retained original production skin stencil through source-triangle barycentric
+weights. Core weights are station-ring means and interior weights are radial
+convex combinations. Interior transport is piecewise linear between the posed
+nodes; it is not a new tissue simulation. `full_vertex_indices` in v2 is only a
+diagnostic dominant source ID; do not use it in place of the attachment arrays.
+
+This entry does not migrate a blood-vessel projection or run the servo. The old
+projection NPZ contains old material addresses and must not be reused with v2.
+The ordinary DMP defaults and original production files remain unchanged.
+The complete point entry includes bundle loading/full node deformation and is
+not certified as a real-time servo cycle.
+
+## Verified scope
+
+Both legs have 62,208 nodes and 322,056 tetrahedra. Independent audits checked
+all spatial tetrahedra, all unwrapped material tetrahedra including periodic
+copies, all 15,336 outer faces, and boundary roundtrips. A fixed-subject SMPL-X
+knee sweep at 0, 15, 30, 45, 60, 75, and 90 degrees passed spatial intersection,
+volume orientation, material-label and layer-order checks. These finite tests
+are not a guarantee for arbitrary body shapes or poses.
+
+The old complete vessel chain is not covered or migrated: its legacy h labels
+include proximal/distal samples outside this numerical range. The endpoint
+expansion trials and full-leg PLC candidates are separate exploratory artifacts.
